              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-8265-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-8265 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Node.js versions before 10.23.1, 12.20.1, 14.15.4, 15.5.1 are vulnerable to a use-after-free bug in its TLS implementation. When writing to a TLS enabled socket, node::StreamBase::Write calls node::TLSWrap::DoWrite with a freshly allocated WriteWrap object as first argument. If the DoWrite method does not return an error, this object is passed back to the caller as part of a StreamWriteResult structure. This may be exploited to corrupt memory leading to a Denial of Service or potentially other exploits."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-8265\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 10.23.1,12.20.1,14.15.4,15.5.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2020-8265](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8265)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2020-8265**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 10.8.0  | 10.23.1,12.20.1,14.15.4,15.5.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2020-8265](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8265)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-8287-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-8287 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Node.js versions before 10.23.1, 12.20.1, 14.15.4, 15.5.1 allow two copies of a header field in an HTTP request (for example, two Transfer-Encoding header fields). In this case, Node.js identifies the first header field and ignores the second. This can lead to HTTP Request Smuggling."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-8287\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: node\nVersion: 10.8.0\nFix Version: 10.23.1,12.20.1,14.15.4,15.5.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2020-8287](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8287)",
